/**
 * A 64 × 64 blue-noise threshold matrix (void-and-cluster, generated offline, seed 0x5ee7),
 * one byte per cell, every value 0..255 present sixteen times. Tiled over the page, it
 * turns a grey image into black-or-white pixels: a pixel is black where its grey is below
 * the cell's threshold. Blue noise puts the dots evenly, with no visible lattice, so a flat
 * light grey reads as a flat light grey and a stroke keeps its whole shape at every shade.
 *
 * Position-keyed and stateless, so two renderers looking at the same grey at the same
 * page position always agree — which is what lets a live preview and a later repaint of
 * the same pixels land identically on a panel. Pure Kotlin.
 */
